messages:
Maria: Heads-up — ran into a Cloudflare Workers compatibility snag while trying to run the JS SDK in a sample app. Issues are around webcrypto + timers + the SDKs retry/auth logic. Workers has no Node timers and limited crypto API surface.

Samir: Can you paste the failing stack or repro steps?

Maria: Sure — quick repro: token refresh triggers setTimeout-based backoff in the SDK, but on Workers we get: "ReferenceError: setTimeout is not defined". Also relying on Nodes crypto.randomBytes for nonce fails (no crypto.randomBytes in Workers). Test snippet: ```js
// inside worker
await client.generate(...); // triggers auth refresh -> backoff -> crash
```

Jules: Oof. We knew timers were a problem w/ some edge RTEs. For crypto, Workers has webcrypto.subtle + crypto.getRandomValues. For timers, we typically convert to promises with AbortController + scheduled alarm via upstream platform (some platforms provide setTimeout, CF historically doesn't).

Kevin: Quick options: 1) Add an official tiny edge shim that swaps Node timers -> microtask or a no-op backoff (risky), and maps randomBytes -> crypto.getRandomValues. 2) Make SDK detect environment and switch to linear/no-wait retries on CRP. 3) Document clearly and ship a sample worker wrapper that provides minimal polyfills.

Maria: I hacked a sketch of minimal polyfill that fixes our case: ```js
// edge-shims.mjs
export function getRandomBytes(n){
  const arr = new Uint8Array(n);
  crypto.getRandomValues(arr);
  return arr;
}
export function backoffDelay(ms){
  // workers: no long timers, just yield control to event loop once
  return Promise.resolve(); // effectively no wait but prevents immediate tight retry loop
}
```
This lets the auth retry code not throw and avoids hammering. Not ideal but small.

Samir: Thats a pragmatic start. We should avoid surprising customers: edge behavior should be explicit. I think we should:
- add an "edge" entrypoint in package exports that uses these shims
- include an official tiny shim package (redwood-edge-shims) for CF/Cloudflare Pages/Netlify edge
- add a sample worker repo and an e2e test in CI that runs on Miniflare/Workers to catch regressions

Jules: Also watch types. TS consumes conditional exports weirdly. If we ship edge.mjs, we need to expose types via typesVersions or an index.d.ts that re-exports types. Otherwise customers get "module not found for types" or duplicate type declarations.

Kevin: Agreed. Proposed project tasks:
1) create redwood-edge-shims package with getRandomBytes + no-op backoff + fetch wrapper for globalThis.fetch if needed (PR: github.com/redwood-inference/examples/pull/123)
2) add conditional exports in package.json: "exports": { "./edge": { "import": "./dist/edge.mjs" }, "./node": { "import": "./dist/node.cjs" } }
3) add types entry: "types": "dist/index.d.ts" and ensure edge builds emit d.ts
4) add a sample Cloudflare Worker repo in examples/edge-worker-auth

DevEx Bot: Created issue #442: "Edge runtime shims + sample: CF webcrypto/timers" and assigned to @samir. CI job suggestion: run unit tests under Miniflare (node 16+).

Maria: One nuance: some customers do want real delays (e.g., exponential backoff to reduce load). Our no-op might make transient retries too aggressive. Maybe allow a configurable strategy: "edgeBackoff: 'noop'|'yield'|'external'" and document tradeoffs.

Samir: Nice. For GA we ship: default to 'yield' (Promise.resolve -> yields once), config opt-in for 'external' where user provides setTimeout polyfill or platform timer. Document recommended pattern for Cloudflare Pages with Workers runtime.

Jules: I'll draft the PR for types + exports and add tests for both ESM/CJS import paths. Kevin — can you sketch the example worker that wires the shim?

Kevin: Yep. Sketch: ```js
import { createClient } from 'redwood';
import { getRandomBytes, backoffDelay } from 'redwood-edge-shims';
const client = createClient({ tokenProvider, backoff: backoffDelay });
addEventListener('fetch', event => event.respondWith(handle(event.request)));
async function handle(req){
  await client.generate(...);
  return new Response('ok');
}
```
I'll open the example PR and link it in the issue.

Maria: Thanks — also propose a short DX doc in docs/edge.md explaining runtime differences and a checklist for onboarding (polyfills, size, allowed timers, local testing with miniflare).

Samir: Sounds like a plan. Action items: Jules PR for exports/types, Kevin PR for example worker, Samir to own shim package + CI job. Maria will draft the docs. Tagging this for next sprint planning. :thumbsup:

DevEx Bot: Note: FYI the SDK has one test failing on Miniflare in nightly; reproducer attached in issue #442.

Maria: I'll follow up in the issue with the failing trace. Thanks all.
